KST records sales completed on your website and gives Kelkoo Group the data needed to measure campaign performance. That data shows which traffic generates the most value for your business so campaigns can be optimised accordingly.

KST data helps Kelkoo Group's optimisation systems determine which:

- traffic sources generate valuable sales;
- placements perform best;
- products and offers should receive more or less traffic.

Complete, accurate sales tracking is therefore essential to effective campaign optimisation.

KST has two components.

**Lead Tag** — loaded on your site to identify visits coming from Kelkoo Group. Once the required consent is given, it stores an anonymous identifier in first-party storage, letting KST recognise a Kelkoo visit if that user later buys.

**Conversion Tag** — fires when an order completes and sends transaction information to Kelkoo Group, such as:

- the order ID;
- the order value;
- the Kelkoo identifier, when available;
- further transaction detail, depending on your implementation.

**Important:** the Conversion Tag should fire for *every* completed order, not only orders you believe came from Kelkoo Group. Kelkoo Group applies its own attribution logic to decide which sales are attributed to Kelkoo traffic. Missing or altered sales data degrades Kelkoo Group's ability to measure and optimise your campaigns.

Because Kelkoo Group uses its own attribution methodology, the number of sales it attributes may differ from figures in Google Analytics or other analytics platforms.

The Conversion Tag sends completed order information to Kelkoo. Add it to your order confirmation (thank-you) page, immediately before the closing `</body>` tag:

```
<script type="text/javascript">
    _kkstrack = {
      merchantInfo : [{ country:'COUNTRY_CODE', merchantId:'MERCHANTID_VALUE' }],
      orderValue: 'ORDER_VALUE',
      orderId: 'ORDER_ID',
      basket:  [{ productname: 'name of product 1',
                 productid: '11111',
                 quantity: '1',
                 price: '4.2'
                },
                { productname: 'name of product 2',
                 productid: '22222',
                 quantity: '3',
                 price: '8.6'
                }
               ]
    };
    (function() {
      var s = document.createElement('script');
      s.type = 'text/javascript';
      s.async = true;
      s.src = 'https://s.kk-resources.com/ks.js';
      var x = document.getElementsByTagName('script')[0];
      x.parentNode.insertBefore(s, x);
    })();
</script>
```

The placeholder values must be replaced with values from your website — some are fixed, others must be populated dynamically per order.

If you run several Kelkoo Group campaigns for the same website, each with its own Merchant ID and/or Country Code, configure them all in the same tag by adding one entry per campaign to the `merchantInfo` array:

```
merchantInfo : [
  {
    country:'fr',
    merchantId:'12941513'
  },
  {
    country:'uk',
    merchantId:'56789'
  }
]
```

After installing, verify both tags work by following the Test Your Kelkoo Sales Tracking Setup guide, confirming that:

- the Lead Tag is loaded on all pages;
- the Conversion Tag is triggered on the order confirmation page;
- the tracking cookie is created correctly;
- conversions are successfully recorded by Kelkoo.

Add this to the end of `web/app/design/frontend/custom/default/template/checkout/success.phtml`, where `custom` is your template name. It retrieves the Order Value and Order Id that KST requires:

```
<?php
  $orderObj = Mage::getModel('sales/order')->loadByIncrementId($this->getOrderId());
  $_totalData =$orderObj->getData();
?>
```

Directly after that code, add the Conversion tag:

```
<script type="text/javascript">
  _kkstrack = {
    merchantInfo : [{ country:'COUNTRY_CODE', merchantId:'MERCHANTID_VALUE' }],
    orderValue: '<?=$_totalData['grand_total'] ?>',
    orderId: '<?=$this->getOrderId() ?>',
    basket:  []
  };
  (function() {
    var s = document.createElement('script');
    s.type = 'text/javascript';
    s.async = true;
    s.src = 'https://s.kk-resources.com/ks.js';
    var x = document.getElementsByTagName('script')[0];
    x.parentNode.insertBefore(s, x);
  })();
</script>
```

`MERCHANTID_VALUE` and `COUNTRY_CODE` can be hard-coded, since they are the same for every sale. `COUNTRY_CODE` is the 2-letter lower-case country code for the country your products are listed under on Kelkoo Group.

1. Log in to your Shopify account.
2. Go to **Settings** → **Customer Events**.
3. Click **Add Custom Pixel**.
4. Name the pixel **Kelkoo Leadtag**.
5. Add this code:

```
(function() {
    var leadTag = document.createElement('script');
    leadTag.src = 'https://s.kk-resources.com/leadtag.js';
    leadTag.async = true;
    document.head.appendChild(leadTag);
})();
```

6. Under **Customer Privacy**, set Permission to **Required Marketing / Analytics**, and Data Sale to **Data Collected does not qualify as data sale**.
7. Scroll to the bottom and select **Connect**.

Create a second pixel the same way, named **Kelkoo Conversion**, using your merchantId and Country Code, with this code:

```
analytics.subscribe("checkout_completed", event => {
  console.log(event.data.checkout);
  var basketFull = [] ;
  var basketContent ;
  for(i = 0 ; i < event.data.checkout.lineItems.length ; i++) {
    basketContent = {} ;
    basketContent.productname = event.data.checkout.lineItems[i].title ;
    basketContent.productid = event.data.checkout.lineItems[i].id ;
    basketContent.quantity = event.data.checkout.lineItems[i].quantity ;
    basketContent.price = event.data.checkout.lineItems[i].variant.price ;
    basketFull.push(basketContent) ;
  }
  _kkstrack = {       
    merchantInfo : [
          {
              country:'ADD YOUR COUNTRY CODE HERE',
              merchantId:'ADD YOUR MERCHANT ID HERE'
          }
      ],     
    orderValue: event.data.checkout.totalPrice.amount,       
    orderId: event.data.checkout.order.id,       
    basket: basketFull     
  };
  (function() {       
    var s = document.createElement('script');       
    s.type = 'text/javascript';       
    s.async = true;       
    s.src = 'https://s.kk-resources.com/ks.js';       
    var x = document.getElementsByTagName('script')[0];       
    x.parentNode.insertBefore(s, x);     
  })(); 
});
```

Under **Customer Privacy**, set Permission to **Not Required** and Data Sale to **Data Collected does not qualify as data sale**, then scroll down and select **Connect**.

Note the privacy setting differs from the Lead Tag, which requires Marketing/Analytics permission.

